§ `Order 13, Rule 1 -- application for injunction or search order`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1239 | 1. —(1) A party may apply for an injunction or a search order, whether or not a claim for such relief was included in that party’s originating process, counterclaim or third party notice, as the case may be. (2) In an urgent case, the claimant may apply for an injunction or a search order before the originating process is issued.
@ref O 13 r 1(1) (src:1239)
GIVEN `the application is for an injunction or a search order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim for such relief was included in the party's originating process, counterclaim or third party notice, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 13 r 1(1) a party may apply for an injunction or a search order` MEANS
    IF `the application is for an injunction or a search order`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "whether or not a claim for such relief was included": the second input does not change the answer
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an injunction or a search order"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

