GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 13 r 1(3) the application may be made in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `o 13 r 1(3) an originating application without notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 13 r 1(3) a summons without notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 13 r 1(3) any other way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be by originating application without notice or summons without notice"; the text does not say that no other way is allowed

-- src:1240 | (3) The application may be by originating application without notice or summons without notice, supported by an affidavit stating the urgency and explaining why the defendant should not be informed about the application and the merits of the application.
@ref O 13 r 1(3) (src:1240)
