    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "supported by an affidavit stating the urgency and explaining why the defendant should not be informed about the application and the merits of the application"; the text does not say what follows without it, and a lawyer could read it as a requirement [marginal-b]

