-- Fork F-O13-1: "including any matter that may affect the merits of the party's case adversely" is read as bringing an adverse matter
-- within the duty whether or not it would be "material" apart from that.
-- src:1242 | (5) A party applying for an injunction or a search order has the duty to disclose to the Court all material facts that the party knows or reasonably ought to know, including any matter that may affect the merits of the party’s case adversely.
@ref O 13 r 1(5) (src:1242)
GIVEN `the party is applying for an injunction or a search order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fact is material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fact is a matter that may affect the merits of the party's case adversely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party knows the fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party reasonably ought to know the fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 13 r 1(5) the party has the duty to disclose the fact to the Court` MEANS
    IF `the party is applying for an injunction or a search order` AND (`the fact is material` OR `the fact is a matter that may affect the merits of the party's case adversely`) AND (`the party knows the fact` OR `the party reasonably ought to know the fact`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all material facts that the party knows or reasonably ought to know, including any matter that may affect the merits of the party's case adversely"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

