-- src:1247 | 2. —(1) The Court may order the detention, custody or preservation of any property which is the subject matter of or may give rise to issues in an action. (2) The Court may order the inspection of any such property in the possession or control of a party.
@ref O 13 r 2(1) (src:1247)
GIVEN `the property is the subject matter of or may give rise to issues in an action` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `o 13 r 2(1) a thing the Court may order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 13 r 2(1) the Court may order this` MEANS
    IF `the property is the subject matter of or may give rise to issues in an action`
    THEN
        CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `o 13 r 2(1) the detention of the property` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 13 r 2(1) the custody of the property` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 13 r 2(1) the preservation of the property` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any property which is the subject matter of or may give rise to issues in an action"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1247 | 2. —(1) The Court may order the detention, custody or preservation of any property which is the subject matter of or may give rise to issues in an action. (2) The Court may order the inspection of any such property in the possession or control of a party.
