§ `Order 13, Rules 5 to 7 -- property held as security; income before trial; immovable property`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1265 | 5. Where the claim is for the recovery of any property held as security, the Court may order the property to be handed over or transferred to the claimant before trial if — ( a )
-- src:1266 | the claimant’s title to the property is not in dispute; and
-- src:1267 | ( b )
-- src:1268 | the claimant pays into Court or provides security for the value of the property or the value of the claim for which the property is held as security, whichever is the lower.
@ref O 13 r 5 (src:1265-1268)
GIVEN valueOfProperty IS A NUMBER
      valueOfClaim IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 13 r 5(b) the amount the claimant must pay into Court or secure` MEANS
    IF valueOfProperty AT MOST valueOfClaim
    THEN valueOfProperty
    ELSE valueOfClaim

-- src:1265 | 5. Where the claim is for the recovery of any property held as security, the Court may order the property to be handed over or transferred to the claimant before trial if — ( a )
-- src:1266 | the claimant’s title to the property is not in dispute; and
-- src:1267 | ( b )
-- src:1268 | the claimant pays into Court or provides security for the value of the property or the value of the claim for which the property is held as security, whichever is the lower.
@ref O 13 r 5 (src:1265-1268)
GIVEN `the claim is for the recovery of any property held as security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's title to the property is not in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the claimant pays into Court or the value of the security the claimant provides` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the claimant must pay into Court or secure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 13 r 5 the Court may order the property to be handed over or transferred to the claimant before trial` MEANS
    IF `the claim is for the recovery of any property held as security`
    THEN
        IF `the claimant's title to the property is not in dispute` AND `the amount the claimant pays into Court or the value of the security the claimant provides` AT LEAST `the amount the claimant must pay into Court or secure`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court may order the property to be handed over or transferred to the claimant before trial if" (a) and (b) (an "if" that fails, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29) [marginal-a]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the claim is for the recovery of any property held as security" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

DECLARE `o 13 r 6 a thing the Court may order` IS ONE OF
    `o 13 r 6(a) the property be used for that purpose before the trial or hearing and the income be kept in an account or be distributed or used for any appropriate purpose`
    `o 13 r 6(b) any part of any movable property be transferred or delivered to all or any of the parties who have an interest in the property`

-- src:1270 | 6. Where the claim involves any property which is capable of generating income, the Court may order that — ( a )
-- src:1271 | the property be used for that purpose before the trial or hearing and the income be kept in an account or be distributed or used for any appropriate purpose; or
-- src:1272 | ( b )
-- src:1273 | any part of any movable property be transferred or delivered to all or any of the parties who have an interest in the property.
@ref O 13 r 6 (src:1270-1273)
GIVEN `the claim involves property which is capable of generating income` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `o 13 r 6 a thing the Court may order`
      `the property is movable property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 13 r 6 the Court may order this` MEANS
    IF `the claim involves property which is capable of generating income`
    THEN
        CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `o 13 r 6(a) the property be used for that purpose before the trial or hearing and the income be kept in an account or be distributed or used for any appropriate purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 13 r 6(b) any part of any movable property be transferred or delivered to all or any of the parties who have an interest in the property` THEN
            IF `the property is movable property`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any part of any movable property" [marginal-b]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the claim involves any property which is capable of generating income" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

